.TH STOP-VNC-SESSION.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-controlroom-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop\-vnc\-session.sh \- stop a control\-room VNC session and its discovery sidecar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stop\-vnc\-session.sh
.I session\-name display
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs on the session host as the session account.
Sends SIGTERM to the pid in
.IR ~/.crs/vnc\-responder\-: display .pid
and removes the file, so the session leaves discovery first, then runs
.B "vncserver \-kill"
.BI : display
if
.B "vncserver \-list"
shows it, else prints
.BR SKIP .
.I session\-name
is used only in messages.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.crs/vnc\-responder\-:N.pid
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1 on a usage error or non\-numeric display; otherwise
.BR vncserver 's
status.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
stop\-vnc\-session.sh shift\-main 2
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-vnc\-session.sh (1),
.BR crs\-remote (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group.
